# The two shapes `pack_spec_go` distinguishes, as an eliminator with an
# abstract motive.
#
# This is what keeps the packing view cheap. Matching the input list directly
# inside `pack_go_view` specialises its goal - which mentions
# `pack_spec_go(xs, xs)` - in all thirty-three branches, and each short branch
# then normalises a padded chunk read with eight limb constructions. That cost
# about a gigabyte of checker memory in every module that imports this one.
# Here the branch motive is an abstract `G`, so nothing is expanded, and the
# recursion below runs on a separate fuel argument instead of on the list.
